{{!--
  Side-menu brand block (see GH issue #8): 40x40 product symbol above the
  product name, gap 24, column layout. Distinct from menu/menu.css's
  `.ids-menu__brand-logo` (row, space-between, border-bottom) which does not
  match the Figma frame — see the issue's own notes on that deviation.

  The symbol has no equivalent in Antora's page model: `site.keys.productLogo`
  is a playbook-level override (same convention as `site.keys.repoUrl` in
  repo-link.hbs), a root-relative or absolute URL to an image. Absent, the
  block renders the product name alone rather than a placeholder mark.

  `site.keys.productLogoDark` is an optional second image for dark mode —
  most single-colour marks (a solid-fill PNG, or an SVG using a literal
  fill/stroke rather than `currentColor`) don't adapt on their own, and
  `currentColor` doesn't help here even if the asset does use it: this is a
  bitmap `<img src>`, not inlined markup (unlike `{{icon}}`'s sprite refs),
  and an externally-referenced SVG document does not inherit CSS from the
  page that embeds it. When a dark variant is configured, both images
  render and side-menu.css swaps between them off the same `.ids-theme-dark`
  root class 08-theme.ts sets (see header.css's theme-toggle icons for the
  identical pattern). When it isn't, the light logo alone renders
  unconditionally — same as before this existed — rather than being hidden
  outright with nothing to replace it.

  Figma only specifies this block at breakpoint l; m/s show it too (icon
  only — the title is already in the header there, see header-content.hbs)
  because a persistent product mark in the menu is worth having regardless
  of what this particular frame drew — see side-menu.css, which hides
  `.side-menu__brand-title` below l. xs gets its own copy of the icon
  inside the drawer's header row instead (nav.hbs) since that breakpoint
  already has its own title + close row; this one stays hidden there.

  One anchor wraps both, not two separate elements, so the link target is
  never lost at a breakpoint that hides the title text.

  It points at `site.homeUrl` — the site's start page (GH-18's landing, where
  one exists) — not at the current component's own landing page. A brand mark
  goes home, everywhere; the component's index is a normal entry in the tree
  below it, and on a single-component site the two were the same URL anyway.
  The component version's own URL stays as the fallback for a playbook with no
  `site.start_page`, where Antora leaves `homeUrl` unset: better a link to the
  component index than the `#` relativize yields for an empty URL.
--}}
<div class="side-menu__brand">
  <a class="side-menu__brand-link" href="{{{relativize (or site.homeUrl page.componentVersion.url)}}}"{{#if page.home}} aria-current="page"{{/if}}>
    {{#with site.keys.productLogo}}
    <img class="side-menu__brand-logo{{#if @root.site.keys.productLogoDark}} side-menu__brand-logo--light{{/if}}" src="{{{relativize this}}}" width="40" height="40" alt="">
    {{/with}}
    {{#with site.keys.productLogoDark}}
    <img class="side-menu__brand-logo side-menu__brand-logo--dark" src="{{{relativize this}}}" width="40" height="40" alt="">
    {{/with}}
    <span class="side-menu__brand-title ids-text ids-text--title-m">{{or page.component.title site.title}}</span>
  </a>
</div>
